  "question": {
    "text": "Let a complex number be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>i</mi></math>. Let&nbsp;another complex number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math> be such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>|</mo><mi>z</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>arg</mi><mfenced><mi>z</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>arg</mi><mfenced><mi>w</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>. Then the area of the&nbsp;triangle (in sq. units) with vertices origin, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>w</mi></math> is equal&nbsp;to",
